/tmp/paper150504778/clustering_2015_05_16.tex:58:Along these lines, convex relaxations provide a framework to attack NP-hard combinatorial problems. This framework is known as the ``relax and round'' paradigm. Given an optimization problem, first relax the feasibility region to a convex set, optimize subject to this larger set, and then round this optimal solution to a point in the original feasibility region. One may seek approximation guarantees in this framework by relating the value of the rounded solution to the value of the optimal solution.
