The paper immediately rules out Track A for the obvious planted-clustering family: its main result says the stated SDP efficiently recovers the planted partition with high probability in exactly that stochastic-ball regime. I’m checking whether it can still be a valid Track B family—i.e., whether solving the SDP is mechanically large while a short structural certificate can be reconstructed and checked exactly.
