The second sweep showed why a three-dimensional cyclic encoding is unsuitable: orthogonality forces a simple coordinate-sum invariant, so an obvious by-hand heuristic solves every instance. I’m replacing that relation with a four-dimensional symplectic quarter-turn, which is orthogonal for every direction but has no forced “sum the coordinates” leak. The shipping witness remains fixed-length; difficulty moves through rational coefficient height.
